{
	title: 'Project discovery and task loading',
	spec: 'From a working directory find the nearest Git root and load tasks/ only when project.ason identifies the Tsk format; derive IDs from flat directories. Require spec rather than description, accept optional boolean once and string-list notes and foldInto, and reject malformed/obsolete fields, invalid status, missing needs, cycles, and missing, self, one-off, or downstream foldInto targets with useful errors. Validate the whole graph before edits, leaving original records intact on invalid input. Support safe tsk del <id>: refuse unknown/referenced tasks (needs or foldInto) and files without --force; explain refusals without changing the project, never follow symlinks or remove unrelated paths. Provide reproducible benchmarks on 1,000/10,000-task graphs, reporting warm lookup and common list/ready queries plus cold startup/loading separately; target under 50 ms warm without weakening validation or brittle timing assertions, and report gaps honestly.',
